--- Scenarios of the KeyMint TA instance (keymint-instance.maude).  Run from the analysis
--- directory:  maude -no-banner keymint-scenarios.maude
---
--- Goal of the attacker: an instance whose boot info is the attacker's value (attV) and whose
--- earlier boot info, set by boot, was lost with a destroyed instance (D = true).
--- Sessions: ss(boot, hal, att).
load keymint-instance

--- S1. boot alone: nobody but boot holds a session.  boot provisions and closes its session (the
--- last one), so the instance with the legitimate boot info is destroyed.  att then opens and sets
--- its own value.  Expect a solution.  No HAL restart or crash is needed.
search [1] in KM-INST : sys(noInst, ss(false, false, false), hist(false, false, false))
    =>* sys(inst(E:Bool, attV), ss(B1:Bool, H1:Bool, A1:Bool), hist(L:Bool, true, P:Bool)) .
show path 1 .

--- S2. the HAL holds a session from the start, and the HAL never closes (KM-INST has no hal close).
--- boot provisions and closes; the HAL's session keeps the instance alive, so the boot info stays.
--- Expect NO solution.
search [1] in KM-INST : sys(inst(true, unset), ss(false, true, false), hist(false, false, false))
    =>* sys(inst(E:Bool, attV), ss(B1:Bool, H1:Bool, A1:Bool), hist(L:Bool, true, P:Bool)) .

--- S3. the same as S2, but the HAL may close its session as the last one (KM-HAL: an HAL restart
--- or crash).  Expect a solution.
search [1] in KM-HAL : sys(inst(true, unset), ss(false, true, false), hist(false, false, false))
    =>* sys(inst(E:Bool, attV), ss(B1:Bool, H1:Bool, A1:Bool), hist(L:Bool, true, P:Bool)) .
show path 1 .

--- S4. att holds a session from the start (it opened the instance before boot).  boot provisions and
--- closes (att keeps the instance alive); then att closes its own session as the last one, which
--- destroys the instance with the legitimate boot info; att reopens and sets its value.
--- Expect a solution: the attack needs no HAL cooperation.
search [1] in KM-INST : sys(inst(true, unset), ss(false, false, true), hist(false, false, false))
    =>* sys(inst(E:Bool, attV), ss(B1:Bool, H1:Bool, A1:Bool), hist(L:Bool, true, P:Bool)) .
show path 1 .

--- S5. race before boot: att opens the TA first and sets its value; the legitimate boot info is then
--- refused (lib.rs:564-580).  Expect a solution (it needs att to open the TA before boot does).
search [1] in KM-INST : sys(noInst, ss(false, false, false), hist(false, false, false))
    =>* sys(inst(E:Bool, attV), ss(B1:Bool, H1:Bool, A1:Bool), hist(L:Bool, D:Bool, false)) .
show path 1 .


--- S6. the HAL holds its session (as kmgk's HAL does), and boot provisions.  Without a TA panic the
--- HAL's session protects the boot info (S2).  With a panic (module KM-PANIC), the instance is destroyed
--- despite the HAL's session; the HAL reconnects to a fresh instance, and att sets its value.
--- Expect a solution: the protection of S2 holds only while the instance never dies.
search [1] in KM-PANIC : sys(inst(true, unset), ss(false, true, false), hist(false, false, false))
    =>* sys(inst(E:Bool, attV), ss(B1:Bool, H1:Bool, A1:Bool), hist(L:Bool, true, P:Bool)) .

quit .
